-## Workflow
-
-1. Select representative workloads from runtime evidence and critical journeys.
-2. Control dataset, environment, toolchain, warmup, cache, concurrency, and background noise.
-3. Measure latency distributions, throughput, errors, CPU, memory, disk, network, GC/runtime, startup, and saturation.
-4. For UI/mobile, include frame time, responsiveness, package size, startup, and energy proxies where feasible.
-5. Use repeated runs and uncertainty intervals.
-6. Compare against target budgets and source baselines without hiding workload changes.
-7. Profile regressions and associate them with migration changes.
-8. Emit pass, fail, blocked, or not-run per budget.
-
