-2. Define valid and invalid input generators from schemas, types, constraints, and observed domains.
-3. Bound generators to avoid unsafe or meaningless states.
-4. Run properties against source, target, and differential harnesses.
-5. Shrink failures and persist minimal counterexamples.
-6. Separate universal properties from assumptions inferred from samples.
-7. Promote confirmed counterexamples into regression fixtures.
-8. Report generator coverage and rejected inputs.
